I agree with a lot of that, but I don't think limiting items is the
path to making a better game.  All it would still take is one good
bones file and your set.

Rather, I think the game, especially in gehennom, needs to supply a
greater range of challenges such that a greater range of equipment
becomes neccisary.

1.  I would make ranged attacks a bigger deal.  Make shields, istead
of an AC bonus, have a % chance to block ranged attacks and make
ranged attacks MUCH more powerful.  Elemental ranged attacks, like
acid or whatnot, have a chance to rot/destroy your shield.

2.  make some areas that are so difficult (think, say, something
equivalent to two demogorgans that are stoning resistant) but with
everything asleep.  Add traps, etc, that will wake them up.

make places with water/pits/lava etc but with a low ceiling such that
mere levitation does not work.


Basically what I wouldn't want is for the player to be nerfed to make
the game harder.  The game should be evolved so that the later game
rises to meet the experienced player and forces them to think outside
their confort zone that has been developed in having their ascension
kit.


